{# ============================================================================
   HOST OVERRIDE of @UhifadhiIncident/report/_drawer.html.twig — the same one
   difference the page override carries: step 3 ("People & evidence", its CAN
   WAIT sub-rows and the "Then, on the record" explainer) is replaced by a single
   quiet line above the File control. Both containers show the same form, so both
   had to change together. Everything else is the module's template verbatim.

   CONTAINER B — THE SLIDE-OVER. Filing FROM a record: another module's prefill
   seam, and the register's report control carrying context.

   SCOPED TO THE CONTENT PANE. The panel comes in from the right edge of the main
   pane at full height, and its dimming backdrop covers exactly that pane — the
   sidebar stays visible on the left and the top bar above. Filing never costs
   anybody their place in the app, only their place on the page.

   THE PAGE BEHIND NEVER GOES AWAY. Under the panel is this area's register, real
   rows and legible, so filing about something you can still see never means
   having to remember it. The panel is narrow on purpose: one column, read top to
   bottom, no two-column form to scan.

   CLOSING IS EXPLICIT, AND ONLY EXPLICIT. The X closes it, and Escape does
   exactly what the X does — including asking first when anything has been typed.
   THE DIMMED REGISTER CLOSES NOTHING: a click that missed the panel may not
   discard a report in progress. Both ways out lead to the same place, and say so:
   back to the record this filing came from.

   IT IS STILL A ROUTE. Reloading re-opens the panel over the same register with
   the same source card, because the container is decided by the address, not by
   a click.

   AND IT IS THE SAME FORM. Every step below is the same partial the full page
   renders, at a narrower width — one set, never two copies.

   Parameters: controller, area, categories, prefill, chosen, csrfToken, errors,
               createUrl, cancelUrl, sourceFiles, behind
   ========================================================================== #}
<div {{ stimulus_controller(controller) }}>
    {# ── THE PAGE BEHIND ─────────────────────────────────────────────────── #}
    <div class="crumb"><a href="{{ path('dashboard_index') }}">uhifadhi</a> / <a href="{{ path('dashboard_area_show', {uuid: area.uuid}) }}">{{ area.name|lower }}</a> / <a href="{{ path('incident_dashboard', {uuid: area.uuid}) }}">incidents</a> / new</div>

    <div class="pghead">
        <div>
            <h1 class="pg">{{ area.name }} — Incidents</h1>
            <p class="pgsub">Filing from {{ prefill.label }}. Its category guess, place, time and note came with it —
                two more answers and the incident exists.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pgact w-pgact">
            <a class="tgl w-act" href="{{ cancelUrl }}">{{ ux_icon('lucide:chevron-left') }} Back without filing</a>
        </div>
    </div>

    {{ include('@UhifadhiIncident/report/_behind.html.twig', {area: area, behind: behind}, with_context: false) }}

    {# ── THE SLIDE-OVER ──────────────────────────────────────────────────── #}
    <div class="ro-slideover" {{ stimulus_target(controller, 'slideover') }}>
        {# THE DIMMED REGISTER DOES NOT CLOSE ANYTHING. It dims and it swallows
           clicks, and that is all: a report in progress may not be discarded by
           a click that missed the panel. Nothing is wired to it. #}
        <div class="ro-slideback"></div>

        <aside class="ro-drawer" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-label="Report an incident">
            <div class="ro-dhd">
                <div>
                    <h3>Report an incident</h3>
                    <p>Two answers and it exists. The rest can follow on the record.</p>
                </div>
                {# A real link, so it works with no JavaScript at all; the
                   controller takes it over to play the panel out and to ask
                   before discarding anything typed. #}
                <a class="x" href="{{ cancelUrl }}" {{ stimulus_action(controller, 'close') }}
                   aria-label="Close without filing">&times;</a>
            </div>

            {# input and change both bubble, so ONE action on the form re-reads the
               gate whatever the filer typed into. #}
            <form class="ro-dform" method="post" action="{{ createUrl }}"
                  {{ stimulus_target(controller, 'form')|stimulus_action(controller, 'gate', 'input')|stimulus_action(controller, 'gate', 'change') }}>
                {{ include('@UhifadhiIncident/report/_carry.html.twig', {csrfToken: csrfToken, prefill: prefill, errors: errors}, with_context: false) }}

                <div class="ro-dbody">
                    {{ include('@UhifadhiIncident/report/_source.html.twig', {prefill: prefill, files: sourceFiles}, with_context: false) }}

                    {{ include('@UhifadhiIncident/report/_secthd.html.twig', {n: 1, heading: 'What kind', mark: 'req', markLabel: 'needed'}, with_context: false) }}
                    {{ include('@UhifadhiIncident/report/_kind.html.twig', {controller: controller, categories: categories, chosen: chosen, compact: true}, with_context: false) }}

                    {{ include('@UhifadhiIncident/report/_secthd.html.twig', {n: 2, heading: 'What happened', mark: null, markLabel: null}, with_context: false) }}
                    {{ include('@UhifadhiIncident/report/_what.html.twig', {controller: controller, categories: categories, chosen: chosen, prefill: prefill, compact: true}, with_context: false) }}

                    {# ONE LINE, NOT A SECTION — the same host ruling the full page
                       carries; see templates/bundles/.../report/_page.html.twig. #}
                    <p class="use">Only the kind, what happened and where are needed now. Severity, people, evidence and
                        money are added on the record afterwards.</p>
                </div>

                {{ include('@UhifadhiIncident/report/_gate.html.twig', {controller: controller, chosen: chosen, prefill: prefill, cancelUrl: cancelUrl, compact: true}, with_context: false) }}
            </form>
        </aside>
    </div>
</div>
